/* The reason macOS shows when Lunaway first asks for the position. Each key
   of Info.plist ending in UsageDescription has a line here and in
   fr.lproj/InfoPlist.strings. */
"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "Lunaway shows your position on the map, sorts the places around you and computes routes from where you are. To compute a route, your position goes to Lunaway's server, which keeps nothing of it. It also goes there when you add a place where you stand.";
